1s89|n|Hazard; danger; peril; exposure to loss, injury, or destruction. ; Hazard of loss; liabillity to loss in property. ; To expose to risk, hazard, or peril; to venture; as, to risk goods on board of a ship; to risk one's person in battle; to risk one's fame by a publication. ; To incur the risk or danger of; as, to risk a battle.	a:12j3,70,4;1lws,40,6;ymp,36,10;ymm,35,14;1w8a,32,3;17w6,25,4;1pns,24,3;1gpw,24,8;16ri,10,3;1c8n,6,5~ymm,35,14;ymp,36,10;1gpw,24,8;1lws,40,6;1c8n,6,5;17w6,25,4;12j3,70,4;16ri,10,3;1w8a,32,3;1pns,24,3	V:9y4,70,6;i1x,43,1~9y4,70,6;i1x,43,1	n:si3,59,7;xsn,43,3;16ri,10,3;ymp,2,1~si3,59,7;16ri,10,3;xsn,43,3;ymp,2,1	N:99g,33,1;rg5,21,1~99g,33,1;rg5,21,1
1s8e|n|	a:18j7,53,3~18j7,53,3	v:22b4,29,3~22b4,29,3	V:55q,75,5;13xz,51,2~55q,75,5;13xz,51,2	n:xsn,72,5;1t3u,69,4~xsn,72,5;1t3u,69,4
1s8f|a|Attended with risk or danger; hazardous.	e:2911,39,7;24gy,37,4;1byh,13,2~2911,39,7;24gy,37,4;1byh,13,2
